1
00:00:27,632 --> 00:00:31,053
THE HUSBAND

2
00:00:35,307 --> 00:00:36,433
THIS SERIES IS FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:36,516 --> 00:00:39,144
CHILDREN WERE FILMED SAFELY
GEN AI WAS USED IN SELECT SCENES

4
00:00:40,103 --> 00:00:41,104
To pick up the money.

5
00:00:41,813 --> 00:00:43,148
What? Money?

6
00:00:43,231 --> 00:00:44,816
The three billion you have here.

7
00:00:45,442 --> 00:00:48,570
I need you to hand it over to me.

8
00:00:48,654 --> 00:00:51,490
Let Seyun go first.
Then I'll give you the money.

9
00:00:52,157 --> 00:00:53,158
No, Mother.

10
00:00:53,241 --> 00:00:56,119
Give me the money first.
That's the only way she'll live.

11
00:00:56,203 --> 00:00:57,746
What?

12
00:00:57,829 --> 00:00:59,206
You greedy bastard.

13
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:03,543
[suspenseful music playing]

14
00:01:21,103 --> 00:01:22,437
Here's your money as promised.

15
00:01:23,772 --> 00:01:24,773
For real this time.

16
00:01:25,607 --> 00:01:27,567
You've gotten pretty smart, Mr. Kang.

17
00:01:29,319 --> 00:01:30,570
All right, Mr. Kang.

18
00:01:31,363 --> 00:01:33,156
Why don't we talk this out?

19
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:36,743
At 8 p.m. tonight,
wait in front of Dong Nam Sports Center.

20
00:01:36,827 --> 00:01:39,705
I'll tell you the exact location then.

21
00:01:45,919 --> 00:01:47,087
Where do I meet you?

22
00:01:49,923 --> 00:01:50,966
[Manhui] Mr. Kang.

23
00:01:51,883 --> 00:01:53,593
Come to Do San Development Company.

24
00:01:54,302 --> 00:01:55,512
You have 10 minutes.

25
00:02:14,573 --> 00:02:15,657
Is this the police?

26
00:02:17,325 --> 00:02:19,119
EPISODE 9

27
00:02:19,202 --> 00:02:22,205
EMERGENCY SERVICES, AMBULANCE

28
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:47,773
-[Dosik] Hey, Choi.
-Yes, sir.

29
00:02:47,856 --> 00:02:48,857
[Hyeonsu] This way.

30
00:02:54,821 --> 00:02:58,366
[breathing heavily]

31
00:02:59,701 --> 00:03:00,786
[Dr. Ko] Critical?

32
00:03:00,869 --> 00:03:03,789
These people are criminals
that did horrible things to my daughter.

33
00:03:03,872 --> 00:03:05,540
How could I let them in my hospital?

34
00:03:07,334 --> 00:03:08,585
You, say something.

35
00:03:09,169 --> 00:03:10,921
Have you forgotten what you've done?

36
00:03:11,004 --> 00:03:14,758
You orchestrated the hit on my daughter,

37
00:03:14,841 --> 00:03:18,428
you broke into my home with a gun
and took three billion won from me.
STYLE
::cue()

38
00:03:19,179 --> 00:03:21,598
You really think you have
any right to be in this room?

39
00:03:21,681 --> 00:03:24,226
Well, I took the money for a reason.

40
00:03:24,893 --> 00:03:26,686
I couldn't tell you at the time.

41
00:03:26,770 --> 00:03:30,106
I was planning to give it back
as soon as I got Seyun back.

42
00:03:30,941 --> 00:03:34,319
Then where's my three billion?

43
00:03:35,362 --> 00:03:36,363
Let me see it now!

44
00:03:37,364 --> 00:03:38,990
I put it in my trunk.

45
00:03:39,824 --> 00:03:41,076
[Dr. Ko] What?

46
00:03:41,159 --> 00:03:44,704
I put it in the trunk
of the car I was driving.

47
00:03:45,789 --> 00:03:47,415
-[Dosik] Check the trunk.
-Yes, sir.

48
00:03:48,250 --> 00:03:51,211
[Dosik] Honestly,
I still don't know what to believe.

49
00:03:51,795 --> 00:03:54,631
Whether you were actually
trying to save your wife,

50
00:03:55,298 --> 00:03:58,218
or you just ended up saving her
when things went sideways.

51
00:03:58,927 --> 00:04:01,471
Let's say you're telling the truth.

52
00:04:01,555 --> 00:04:04,391
But what about the money?
Where is that three billion?

53
00:04:04,975 --> 00:04:07,894
I told you. I left it in the trunk.

54
00:04:07,978 --> 00:04:10,188
We searched the whole thing
but found nothing.

55
00:04:11,231 --> 00:04:13,400
So be honest with us, Mr. Kang.

56
00:04:13,483 --> 00:04:17,612
If what you said were true,
the money would've been in the trunk.

57
00:04:19,823 --> 00:04:22,534
We don't know what else we'll find,
so search every inch.

58
00:04:22,617 --> 00:04:23,618
[Hyeonsu] Yes, sir.

59
00:04:27,163 --> 00:04:28,206
What's that?

60
00:04:28,290 --> 00:04:30,542
It's a cell phone.
It was under the fridge.

61
00:04:31,376 --> 00:04:32,586
-[Dosik] The fridge?
-Yeah.

62
00:04:32,669 --> 00:04:33,795
[Hyeonsu] Captain.

63
00:04:34,963 --> 00:04:36,172
You should see this.

64
00:04:36,256 --> 00:04:38,884
COME TO THE HOSPITAL
WE NEED TO TALK

65
00:04:38,967 --> 00:04:40,010
[Dosik] "To the hospital"?

66
00:04:40,594 --> 00:04:43,471
-Is that all?
-Yeah, everything else was wiped clean.

67
00:04:44,931 --> 00:04:47,976
[sighs] Get Kim Gyeongae's phone
to Forensics now.

68
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:50,478
And track down the owner of this number.

69
00:04:51,938 --> 00:04:53,315
What?

70
00:04:53,398 --> 00:04:55,442
Kang Taeju was there?

71
00:04:56,234 --> 00:04:57,694
Why are you telling me this now?

72
00:04:58,445 --> 00:05:01,489
I'll take care of it myself.
Just come to the hospital.

73
00:05:05,076 --> 00:05:08,038
Darn, Kang Taeju.
If only he hadn't shown up.

74
00:05:08,121 --> 00:05:10,206
[phone buzzing]

75
00:05:10,290 --> 00:05:13,084
INCOMING CALL

76
00:05:16,504 --> 00:05:19,674
[buzzing continues]

77
00:05:39,402 --> 00:05:40,570
[phone buzzes]

78
00:05:46,576 --> 00:05:49,329
PROCEED AS PLANNED

79
00:05:52,749 --> 00:05:54,250
[sighs]

80
00:05:56,711 --> 00:05:57,921
[phone buzzes]

81
00:05:59,172 --> 00:06:00,173
MESSAGES
NEW MESSAGE

82
00:06:04,135 --> 00:06:06,554
[tense music playing]

83
00:06:20,694 --> 00:06:21,695
Honey.

84
00:06:23,238 --> 00:06:24,656
Hang in there.

85
00:06:24,739 --> 00:06:29,661
THE HUSBAND
STYLE
::cue()

86
00:06:34,374 --> 00:06:38,128
FORENSICS
POLICE

87
00:06:39,462 --> 00:06:40,505
POTASSIUM CHLORIDE

88
00:07:07,198 --> 00:07:09,701
NS: NEUROSURGERY
HA JEONGSOO

89
00:07:09,784 --> 00:07:12,203
DO NOT CROSS, POLICE LINE
UNDER INVESTIGATION

90
00:07:12,287 --> 00:07:14,497
[indistinct radio chatter]

91
00:07:20,587 --> 00:07:24,007
You came down here, looking for
Ha Jeongsoo and called his phone,

92
00:07:24,716 --> 00:07:27,010
you heard his phone ringing
by the emergency stairs,

93
00:07:27,510 --> 00:07:30,180
and found him collapsed there.

94
00:07:30,263 --> 00:07:31,264
Is that correct?

95
00:07:31,347 --> 00:07:32,599
[Taeju] Yeah, that's correct.

96
00:07:34,017 --> 00:07:36,269
[Dosik] But why were you
looking for him anyway?

97
00:07:36,352 --> 00:07:39,189
[footsteps approaching]

98
00:07:41,274 --> 00:07:43,318
What… Is it true?

99
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:45,445
Dr. Ha is dead?

100
00:07:46,529 --> 00:07:47,530
Yes.

101
00:07:49,824 --> 00:07:51,367
I need to see him myself.

102
00:07:51,451 --> 00:07:53,953
[stammers]
Forensics is in there right now.

103
00:07:54,037 --> 00:07:55,330
You're not allowed.

104
00:07:59,793 --> 00:08:00,794
Are you okay?

105
00:08:01,753 --> 00:08:02,754
Yeah.

106
00:08:03,254 --> 00:08:04,756
[Dr. Ko] How did Dr. Ha end up…

107
00:08:04,839 --> 00:08:07,133
What in the world happened?

108
00:08:08,676 --> 00:08:11,012
-We're looking into that right now.
-[Dr. Ko sighs]

109
00:08:11,095 --> 00:08:15,934
Director Ko should be able to tell you
a lot more about Dr. Ha than I can.

110
00:08:16,017 --> 00:08:17,519
[mysterious music playing]

111
00:08:23,858 --> 00:08:26,402
He was going to meet Dr. Ha last night.

112
00:08:29,030 --> 00:08:30,114
Is that correct?

113
00:08:30,865 --> 00:08:32,450
I… Well…

114
00:08:33,368 --> 00:08:37,163
He called out of the blue last night
about an emergency,

115
00:08:38,206 --> 00:08:41,000
so I came to the hospital like he asked.

116
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:45,630
But when I arrived, I couldn't find him.

117
00:08:46,339 --> 00:08:47,799
I couldn't reach him either,

118
00:08:48,842 --> 00:08:50,009
so…

119
00:08:50,093 --> 00:08:53,513
I went back home after a while.

120
00:08:55,390 --> 00:08:56,391
What?

121
00:08:57,559 --> 00:08:59,227
What are you saying?

122
00:08:59,727 --> 00:09:01,813
[scoffs] Calm down.

123
00:09:01,896 --> 00:09:03,565
I can't understand a word!

124
00:09:03,648 --> 00:09:04,774
[sighs]

125
00:09:05,733 --> 00:09:08,403
You know what a huge problem
you've caused?

126
00:09:09,070 --> 00:09:10,613
Where are you right now?

127
00:09:10,697 --> 00:09:14,075
No. Just come back to the hospital!

128
00:09:14,159 --> 00:09:15,160
[gasps]

129
00:09:18,454 --> 00:09:21,457
-[phone buzzes]
-[Dosik] Detective Oh. Yeah, got it.

130
00:09:22,917 --> 00:09:24,961
I'm going to check
the surveillance footage.

131
00:09:25,044 --> 00:09:26,212
Give me a minute.

132
00:09:26,296 --> 00:09:28,381
[gasps] I'll go with you.

133
00:09:29,674 --> 00:09:30,800
Be right back.

134
00:09:36,097 --> 00:09:38,308
[music intensifies]

135
00:09:48,193 --> 00:09:49,527
[music ends]
STYLE
::cue()

136
00:09:49,611 --> 00:09:52,113
This is the parking garage last night.

137
00:09:52,197 --> 00:09:56,910
SECTOR A

138
00:09:58,161 --> 00:10:00,455
And this is after Mr. Ha walked past.

139
00:10:01,789 --> 00:10:03,833
First comes Director Ko.

140
00:10:05,835 --> 00:10:07,086
This is the parking area.

141
00:10:14,427 --> 00:10:15,929
Next comes Mr. Kang.

142
00:10:21,059 --> 00:10:23,478
-Yeah, it's just like Mr. Kang said.
-Right.

143
00:10:26,564 --> 00:10:30,235
And this is Mr. Ha taking the elevator
up to the hospital.

144
00:10:30,318 --> 00:10:34,280
MAIN BUILDING E/V #3

145
00:10:38,993 --> 00:10:40,828
[no audible dialogue]

146
00:10:45,250 --> 00:10:46,334
[Dosik] Hold on.

147
00:10:46,918 --> 00:10:48,336
Did he go right back down?

148
00:10:48,419 --> 00:10:49,420
[Detective Oh] Yeah.

149
00:10:50,129 --> 00:10:53,091
Who was that on the elevator with him?

150
00:10:57,804 --> 00:10:59,222
Dr. Cha Myeonghui.

151
00:11:02,058 --> 00:11:04,978
To be honest,
I was a bit stunned when I got the call.

152
00:11:06,938 --> 00:11:10,566
I had no idea that Dr. Ha
would do anything like that.

153
00:11:11,150 --> 00:11:16,698
So, you were on the elevator
with him last night, correct?

154
00:11:17,991 --> 00:11:18,992
Yes.

155
00:11:19,075 --> 00:11:22,996
Would you mind telling us
what you guys talked about?

156
00:11:23,705 --> 00:11:27,041
I said hi to him,
but he didn't say anything.

157
00:11:27,959 --> 00:11:31,671
He didn't look so well,
so I asked if he was okay.

158
00:11:31,754 --> 00:11:33,047
So, what did he say?

159
00:11:33,673 --> 00:11:35,508
He just said he was fine.

160
00:11:36,968 --> 00:11:39,721
But something was off about him.

161
00:11:40,513 --> 00:11:44,100
It sounded like he was
talking to himself under his breath.

162
00:11:44,183 --> 00:11:45,476
Talking to himself?

163
00:11:46,436 --> 00:11:47,812
Do you know what he was saying?

164
00:11:48,730 --> 00:11:50,106
Uh…

165
00:11:50,189 --> 00:11:52,608
I didn't quite make out
what he was saying.

166
00:11:53,276 --> 00:11:55,820
I just told him to come to me
if he's struggling.

167
00:11:56,612 --> 00:11:59,449
That's all I could do for him.

168
00:12:00,366 --> 00:12:03,453
I had no idea that would be the last time.

169
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:07,832
Well, do you happen to know
why he took the same elevator down

170
00:12:07,915 --> 00:12:09,042
to the basement?

171
00:12:10,752 --> 00:12:13,921
No, I got off before that,
so I don't know.

172
00:12:14,005 --> 00:12:16,466
[Dosik] Right. Of course.

173
00:12:17,175 --> 00:12:21,137
So what was he like on an average day?

174
00:12:21,721 --> 00:12:22,805
Anything peculiar?

175
00:12:23,514 --> 00:12:28,144
It's hard to say for sure
since we never had a formal consultation.

176
00:12:28,227 --> 00:12:30,396
But the past few times
I ran into him recently,

177
00:12:31,397 --> 00:12:33,358
he did seem a bit on edge.

178
00:12:34,359 --> 00:12:36,069
I wouldn't say he was anxious,

179
00:12:36,152 --> 00:12:39,489
but like he had a lot
weighing on his mind.

180
00:12:42,742 --> 00:12:43,743
All right.

181
00:12:44,327 --> 00:12:46,788
And thank you for your time.

182
00:12:46,871 --> 00:12:49,749
I'll let you know if I remember
anything that might help.

183
00:12:49,832 --> 00:12:51,084
You can call me anytime.

184
00:12:51,709 --> 00:12:53,628
Yeah, we appreciate it.
STYLE
::cue()

185
00:13:06,516 --> 00:13:11,187
MAJOR CRIMES UNIT 2

186
00:13:14,148 --> 00:13:15,191
[Detective Oh] You're back.

187
00:13:15,691 --> 00:13:17,652
Captain, we got the autopsy results.

188
00:13:18,861 --> 00:13:20,822
SUSPECT PROFILE
NAME: KIM GYEONGAE

189
00:13:20,905 --> 00:13:23,533
[suspenseful music playing]

190
00:13:27,453 --> 00:13:29,539
CARDIAC ARREST FROM
POTASSIUM CHLORIDE INJECTION

191
00:13:29,622 --> 00:13:31,749
[exhales deeply]

192
00:13:31,833 --> 00:13:34,252
Captain, I think you should see this.

193
00:13:34,335 --> 00:13:35,586
What is it?

194
00:13:35,670 --> 00:13:38,589
About the phone
that Ha Jeongsoo had on him…

195
00:13:38,673 --> 00:13:39,674
Yeah.

196
00:13:39,757 --> 00:13:42,009
It's the same number
that contacted Kim Gyeongae.

197
00:13:42,718 --> 00:13:44,303
-What?
-And here.

198
00:13:45,513 --> 00:13:48,474
They texted each other
on the date of Ms. Ko Seyun's abduction.

199
00:13:51,853 --> 00:13:53,062
SEONGJIN POLICE STATION

200
00:13:53,146 --> 00:13:56,399
[Dosik] Why were you looking for Mr. Ha?

201
00:13:57,191 --> 00:13:58,901
I had to ask him something.

202
00:13:59,485 --> 00:14:00,611
Ask him what?

203
00:14:01,779 --> 00:14:02,989
Kim Gyeongae…

204
00:14:05,158 --> 00:14:06,826
Why he tried to kill her.

205
00:14:07,326 --> 00:14:08,828
He tried to kill her?

206
00:14:09,912 --> 00:14:11,164
What do you mean by that?

207
00:14:12,415 --> 00:14:14,333
Two nights ago,

208
00:14:15,168 --> 00:14:19,255
I found him in her room and he had
a vial of potassium chloride in his hands.

209
00:14:19,338 --> 00:14:20,923
Potassium chloride?

210
00:14:21,424 --> 00:14:25,094
I barely stopped him from injecting it
into her IV without dilution.

211
00:14:25,178 --> 00:14:27,847
[mysterious music playing]

212
00:14:33,644 --> 00:14:35,271
COME TO THE HOSPITAL
WE NEED TO TALK

213
00:14:35,354 --> 00:14:37,940
[Dosik] This message is from the phone
we found on Mr. Ha Jeongsoo.

214
00:14:38,024 --> 00:14:40,943
He sent it to Kim Gyeongae
on the day your wife was abducted.

215
00:14:42,236 --> 00:14:44,780
It seems he used this phone
only for contacting her.

216
00:14:44,864 --> 00:14:49,076
Mr. Ha was keeping her
updated on your movements, Mr. Kang.

217
00:14:52,121 --> 00:14:53,122
What's wrong?

218
00:14:57,460 --> 00:15:00,296
Dr. Ha told me that day at the hospital

219
00:15:00,379 --> 00:15:02,173
that he was only…

220
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:06,844
doing as he was told.

221
00:15:06,928 --> 00:15:08,221
[Dosik] "Doing as he was told"?

222
00:15:08,846 --> 00:15:13,559
You mean someone else
put him up to kill Kim Gyeongae?

223
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:19,523
That's what I'm not sure about.

224
00:15:20,650 --> 00:15:23,444
I went back
to the hospital to find that out.

225
00:15:25,154 --> 00:15:27,490
[music ends]

226
00:15:27,573 --> 00:15:29,492
[monitor beeping]

227
00:15:30,243 --> 00:15:31,244
Ms. Kim.

228
00:15:32,662 --> 00:15:34,497
Ms. Kim? Can you hear me at all?

229
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:35,581
Yeah.

230
00:15:35,665 --> 00:15:37,667
-[groans]
-[knocks on door]

231
00:15:37,750 --> 00:15:39,877
[sliding door opens]

232
00:15:40,628 --> 00:15:42,088
[Dosik] How's it going?

233
00:15:42,171 --> 00:15:44,173
-Hi.
-How's she looking?

234
00:15:44,257 --> 00:15:48,177
She's regained consciousness,
but she's still a bit out of it.

235
00:15:50,554 --> 00:15:51,555
Ms. Kim Gyeongae?

236
00:15:52,473 --> 00:15:53,474
We're with the police.

237
00:15:56,477 --> 00:16:00,356
[stammers]
This thing is a bit uncomfortable.

238
00:16:00,439 --> 00:16:02,358
You're currently under arrest.

239
00:16:02,942 --> 00:16:04,485
And your husband is a wanted man.

240
00:16:05,278 --> 00:16:08,155
Ms. Kim, why did you kidnap Ms. Ko Seyun?

241
00:16:12,368 --> 00:16:13,494
Ms. Kim.

242
00:16:14,704 --> 00:16:17,039
What was the purpose
of kidnapping Ko Seyun?

243
00:16:17,123 --> 00:16:20,376
Detective? The patient has
just regained consciousness.

244
00:16:21,043 --> 00:16:23,671
She needs rest
more than anything right now.

245
00:16:23,754 --> 00:16:25,673
Maybe you should continue another time.

246
00:16:26,799 --> 00:16:30,094
[monitor beeping continues]

247
00:16:32,596 --> 00:16:34,056
-Fair enough.
-Thank you.

248
00:16:35,516 --> 00:16:37,893
Both my husband and I…

249
00:16:40,229 --> 00:16:43,524
we were just pawns in this game.

250
00:16:44,025 --> 00:16:46,569
[eerie music playing]

251
00:16:47,737 --> 00:16:50,323
An update on
the major hospital kidnapping case.

252
00:16:50,406 --> 00:16:52,658
-Kidnapping?
-Police investigation has revealed

253
00:16:52,742 --> 00:16:55,202
that a doctor at the facility,
identified as Suspect B,

254
00:16:55,286 --> 00:16:57,997
ordered accomplice A
to kidnap the hospital chairwoman,

255
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,832
-the director's daughter.
-My gosh.

256
00:16:59,915 --> 00:17:03,294
Suspect B was reportedly struggling
with multi-million-won private debt,
STYLE
::cue()

257
00:17:03,377 --> 00:17:06,839
and police now believe he took
his own life after the plot failed.

258
00:17:06,922 --> 00:17:08,883
Gosh, I feel so bad for Dr. Kang.

259
00:17:08,966 --> 00:17:11,552
The police were after him for days
when he was innocent.

260
00:17:12,345 --> 00:17:15,056
He looked like he had
wounds all over his body too.

261
00:17:15,139 --> 00:17:17,308
See? I told you.

262
00:17:17,391 --> 00:17:20,811
I said, Dr. Kang would never do
something like that, didn't I?

263
00:17:21,437 --> 00:17:23,189
But can you believe that about Dr. Ha?

264
00:17:23,272 --> 00:17:24,774
We used to see him every day here.

265
00:17:24,857 --> 00:17:27,985
He seemed so gentle.
But he was up to something so horrible?

266
00:17:28,069 --> 00:17:32,948
I mean, he made a lot of mistakes,
so I just thought he was a bit clumsy.

267
00:17:33,532 --> 00:17:35,368
Guess you can never really know someone.

268
00:17:35,951 --> 00:17:37,662
You're such a bad judge of character.

269
00:17:38,371 --> 00:17:40,414
I always knew he was trouble.

270
00:17:40,498 --> 00:17:42,041
That look in his eyes was…

271
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:45,503
You know, he always seemed a bit on edge.

272
00:17:45,586 --> 00:17:47,171
Like he was nervous.

273
00:17:47,254 --> 00:17:50,132
The investigation into the high-profile
hospital kidnapping case,

274
00:17:50,216 --> 00:17:52,343
which shocked the public,
has taken a major turn.

275
00:17:52,426 --> 00:17:54,929
Suspect A, who has regained
consciousness after surgery,

276
00:17:55,012 --> 00:17:56,389
reportedly testified to police

277
00:17:56,472 --> 00:17:59,517
that they followed Suspect B's orders.

278
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,519
Meanwhile, Dr. Kang,
who was once named a suspect…

279
00:18:01,602 --> 00:18:03,229
[doorbell rings]

280
00:18:03,312 --> 00:18:05,731
…has suffered from an overreaching
police investigation. Consequently--

281
00:18:12,029 --> 00:18:14,281
FRONT DOOR
SAVE, OPEN

282
00:18:25,584 --> 00:18:26,794
How are you feeling?

283
00:18:29,130 --> 00:18:30,256
Well, I'm fine,

284
00:18:30,339 --> 00:18:32,883
but what brings you out here?

285
00:18:32,967 --> 00:18:35,594
[Dosik] I wanted to apologize
for suspecting you.

286
00:18:35,678 --> 00:18:38,806
So I wanted to sit down
and have a cup of coffee with you.

287
00:18:40,015 --> 00:18:41,016
[Taeju] Yeah.

288
00:18:43,644 --> 00:18:45,396
You're not a very good liar.

289
00:18:47,940 --> 00:18:49,775
If you want to say something, say it.

290
00:18:53,738 --> 00:18:56,866
Once we find Noh Manhui, who's on the run,
this case will be closed.

291
00:18:59,702 --> 00:19:00,703
It's just that…

292
00:19:01,579 --> 00:19:02,663
it doesn't quite add up.

293
00:19:04,999 --> 00:19:07,251
Are you talking about Dr. Ha Jeongsoo?

294
00:19:11,088 --> 00:19:14,091
He said that he was only doing
as he was told.

295
00:19:15,092 --> 00:19:16,927
At first, I thought he was just lying

296
00:19:17,428 --> 00:19:19,096
to save his own skin.

297
00:19:20,222 --> 00:19:23,976
But the evidence fits together too neatly,
like someone set it all up.

298
00:19:24,059 --> 00:19:25,311
I can't put my finger on it,

299
00:19:26,103 --> 00:19:27,521
but it just doesn't feel right.

300
00:19:29,148 --> 00:19:31,484
It's as if I'm missing something.

301
00:19:33,819 --> 00:19:34,820
But then…

302
00:19:36,697 --> 00:19:38,741
your face tells me I'm not the only one.

303
00:19:42,369 --> 00:19:44,038
If you ever think of something,

304
00:19:45,039 --> 00:19:46,165
please let me know.

305
00:19:48,667 --> 00:19:49,668
Okay.

306
00:19:51,462 --> 00:19:54,465
[tense music playing]

307
00:20:13,484 --> 00:20:15,903
[monitor beeping]

308
00:20:26,580 --> 00:20:28,541
If that's the case, I'd like to wait.

309
00:20:28,624 --> 00:20:29,834
Very well. [chuckles]

310
00:20:31,585 --> 00:20:34,004
Thank you, Dr. Ko. We're in your hands.

311
00:20:34,755 --> 00:20:35,756
Honey.

312
00:20:38,843 --> 00:20:41,095
[Dr. Ko] Hmm. [grunts]

313
00:20:58,654 --> 00:20:59,697
[music ends]
STYLE
::cue()

314
00:20:59,780 --> 00:21:01,699
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

315
00:21:01,782 --> 00:21:02,867
[Dr. Ko sighs]

316
00:21:03,993 --> 00:21:06,287
I believe the incident involving Dr. Ha

317
00:21:06,370 --> 00:21:09,039
has come
as a tremendous shock to all of us,

318
00:21:09,123 --> 00:21:13,335
including our medical staff
and everyone else involved.

319
00:21:15,045 --> 00:21:18,841
[sighs] This case may have come to an end,

320
00:21:19,425 --> 00:21:21,844
but the patients remain uneasy.

321
00:21:22,553 --> 00:21:27,349
Our priority should be
getting the hospital back on track.

322
00:21:27,933 --> 00:21:29,184
Which is why…

323
00:21:30,311 --> 00:21:31,770
[door closes]

324
00:21:31,854 --> 00:21:33,647
My apologies for being late.

325
00:21:40,487 --> 00:21:41,530
Sorry.

326
00:21:41,614 --> 00:21:43,157
Don't mind me.

327
00:21:44,742 --> 00:21:45,951
[Dr. Ko grunts]

328
00:21:46,619 --> 00:21:47,620
Uh…

329
00:21:48,203 --> 00:21:50,539
An arrest warrant has been issued
for Kim Gyeongae,

330
00:21:50,623 --> 00:21:53,000
who is currently our patient.

331
00:21:53,584 --> 00:21:56,754
As soon as she's stable,
she'll be transferred into police custody.

332
00:21:57,338 --> 00:21:59,089
In the meantime,

333
00:21:59,173 --> 00:22:03,260
I'd like Dr. Choi Chiung
to oversee her care.

334
00:22:04,011 --> 00:22:05,512
May I take over?

335
00:22:05,596 --> 00:22:08,015
[tense music playing]

336
00:22:08,098 --> 00:22:09,099
[Dr. Ko] Excuse me?

337
00:22:09,892 --> 00:22:11,101
I was asking

338
00:22:12,853 --> 00:22:15,230
if I could take point
on Kim Gyeongae's case, sir.

339
00:22:15,814 --> 00:22:17,232
Are you being serious right now?

340
00:22:18,150 --> 00:22:19,818
I operated on her.

341
00:22:20,861 --> 00:22:25,324
No one here knows her post-op course
and current condition better than I do.

342
00:22:26,825 --> 00:22:31,121
It makes more sense to keep me on her case
than pulling someone else in.

343
00:22:31,747 --> 00:22:35,417
With everything that's going on,
if you stay on this case,

344
00:22:35,501 --> 00:22:37,294
it'll only get people talking.

345
00:22:38,796 --> 00:22:40,005
Isn't it weirder to change

346
00:22:40,089 --> 00:22:42,591
attending physicians
just because people might talk?

347
00:22:44,343 --> 00:22:47,805
If there's anyone here who knows
about this patient better than I do,

348
00:22:47,888 --> 00:22:49,264
I'm happy to step aside.

349
00:22:56,105 --> 00:22:58,107
Otherwise, I'm staying on her case.

350
00:23:05,656 --> 00:23:07,866
[music intensifies]

351
00:23:13,998 --> 00:23:15,207
How are you feeling?

352
00:23:17,251 --> 00:23:19,503
Wait, what's going on?

353
00:23:20,337 --> 00:23:21,547
What are you doing here?

354
00:23:21,630 --> 00:23:24,258
Acute bleeding developed around the tumor,

355
00:23:24,341 --> 00:23:26,260
so we had to perform an emergency surgery.

356
00:23:26,802 --> 00:23:30,264
The trauma caused the tumor to hemorrhage,
which compressed your nerves.

357
00:23:30,347 --> 00:23:33,142
We were able to drain the blood
and relieve that pressure.

358
00:23:33,225 --> 00:23:34,768
You should start improving now.

359
00:23:34,852 --> 00:23:37,855
Is that what you're here to talk about?

360
00:23:37,938 --> 00:23:40,399
Oh, I'll be your attending physician
starting today.

361
00:23:40,482 --> 00:23:42,443
[scoffs, laughs]

362
00:23:42,526 --> 00:23:43,861
What did you just say?

363
00:23:45,362 --> 00:23:46,989
Thanks to your testimony,

364
00:23:47,656 --> 00:23:49,158
my name was cleared,

365
00:23:49,241 --> 00:23:50,993
-and I'm back at the hospital.
-[scoffs]

366
00:23:51,076 --> 00:23:53,495
It only feels right that I take your case.

367
00:23:54,288 --> 00:23:55,748
Just cut to the chase.

368
00:23:56,457 --> 00:23:58,083
What do you really want?

369
00:23:59,918 --> 00:24:02,671
You said Dr. Ha

370
00:24:03,380 --> 00:24:05,549
planned this whole thing by himself.

371
00:24:07,301 --> 00:24:08,886
But I just don't get it.

372
00:24:09,887 --> 00:24:12,097
The fact that you don't understand it

373
00:24:12,765 --> 00:24:14,725
doesn't make it any less true.

374
00:24:15,726 --> 00:24:20,022
I don't get why Dr. Ha did
what he did to me either.

375
00:24:26,862 --> 00:24:29,198
Remember what you said to me
before your surgery?
STYLE
::cue()

376
00:24:31,116 --> 00:24:32,326
You mean…

377
00:24:33,994 --> 00:24:37,956
"Extending other people's lifespans
by using those unborn babies."

378
00:24:39,083 --> 00:24:40,084
You mean that?

379
00:24:40,167 --> 00:24:41,543
About the fetal stem cells?

380
00:24:43,504 --> 00:24:44,713
How do you know about that?

381
00:24:44,797 --> 00:24:48,258
I signed up for the clinical trial
at this hospital.

382
00:24:48,342 --> 00:24:50,344
That's when I found out
what it was all about.

383
00:24:51,095 --> 00:24:52,471
But who cares, right?

384
00:24:52,971 --> 00:24:54,515
As long as I could get on the list.

385
00:24:55,390 --> 00:24:59,061
At first, I thought,
"How could he call himself a doctor?"

386
00:25:01,438 --> 00:25:04,066
But I was in no position to judge.

387
00:25:05,317 --> 00:25:06,568
What I didn't know

388
00:25:07,694 --> 00:25:11,782
was that he planned
to take advantage of us for his own good.

389
00:25:15,661 --> 00:25:18,747
That answers your question, doesn't it?

390
00:25:24,086 --> 00:25:25,295
This is unfair!

391
00:25:25,379 --> 00:25:27,673
I'm a victim in all of this too!

392
00:25:29,383 --> 00:25:31,301
If I had gotten that surgery,

393
00:25:32,052 --> 00:25:34,096
I wouldn't have taken things this far.

394
00:25:35,389 --> 00:25:36,390
But guess what?

395
00:25:38,475 --> 00:25:39,518
I didn't make the cut.

396
00:25:40,602 --> 00:25:43,897
My life was at stake,
but they made it sound so simple.

397
00:25:44,731 --> 00:25:47,734
There was no rhyme or reason to any of it.

398
00:25:50,571 --> 00:25:55,242
They dropped me from the surgery list
just because I'm an ex-con.

399
00:25:56,034 --> 00:26:00,205
They ruled you out
because of your criminal record?

400
00:26:01,874 --> 00:26:03,458
Who told you that?

401
00:26:04,877 --> 00:26:05,961
Was that Dr. Ha as well?

402
00:26:06,503 --> 00:26:09,131
[mysterious music playing]

403
00:26:10,841 --> 00:26:13,010
Well, what does any of that matter now?

404
00:26:15,012 --> 00:26:16,555
It's all in the past.

405
00:26:17,472 --> 00:26:20,851
You should let it go, Doctor.

406
00:26:22,769 --> 00:26:23,770
All right.

407
00:26:24,897 --> 00:26:26,356
I'll see you on my next rounds.

408
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:28,275
Take good care of yourself.

409
00:26:30,485 --> 00:26:32,696
[music intensifies]

410
00:26:42,247 --> 00:26:43,373
[music stops]

411
00:26:45,083 --> 00:26:47,961
[Gyeongae] There was no rhyme
or reason to any of it.

412
00:26:48,545 --> 00:26:53,050
They dropped me from the surgery list
just because I'm an ex-con.

413
00:26:53,133 --> 00:26:55,344
[music resumes]

414
00:27:00,474 --> 00:27:01,642
Hey, it's me.

415
00:27:01,725 --> 00:27:03,060
I have a favor to ask.

416
00:27:22,829 --> 00:27:24,665
[music intensifies]

417
00:27:57,280 --> 00:27:58,490
[music ends]
STYLE
::cue()

418
00:28:04,871 --> 00:28:06,039
Hey, Dr. Kang.

419
00:28:07,207 --> 00:28:08,208
What brings you here?

420
00:28:08,291 --> 00:28:10,961
I just had to take a look at something.

421
00:28:13,338 --> 00:28:14,339
I see.

422
00:28:15,132 --> 00:28:16,842
Right, see you around.

423
00:28:22,180 --> 00:28:23,724
[card reader beeps]

424
00:28:32,232 --> 00:28:33,692
[Taeju] Thanks. Appreciate it.

425
00:28:34,192 --> 00:28:36,069
What did you need the lab keycard for?

426
00:28:38,113 --> 00:28:39,740
I just had to look into something.

427
00:28:40,866 --> 00:28:41,950
What was it?

428
00:28:42,534 --> 00:28:47,664
It turns out, Kim Gyeongae signed up
for one of our clinical trials.

429
00:28:48,957 --> 00:28:50,834
-Clinical trial?
-Yeah.

430
00:28:50,917 --> 00:28:53,712
It might have something
to do with your getting kidnapped,

431
00:28:54,546 --> 00:28:58,216
so I wanted to look at some applications
and selection records,

432
00:28:58,300 --> 00:28:59,468
but they weren't there.

433
00:29:00,510 --> 00:29:01,970
I'm sure I've seen them there.

434
00:29:03,764 --> 00:29:05,265
Are you saying someone took them?

435
00:29:06,808 --> 00:29:10,812
Seyun, would you mind
looking into your father's study

436
00:29:11,605 --> 00:29:17,360
and seeing if you find any applications
or selection records in there?

437
00:29:21,156 --> 00:29:22,824
Is that what this was?

438
00:29:23,617 --> 00:29:26,953
Is that why you showed up
at my parents' house?

439
00:29:27,954 --> 00:29:29,372
Is this all…

440
00:29:32,250 --> 00:29:34,169
Is it related to my dad somehow?

441
00:29:34,795 --> 00:29:37,089
[cryptic music playing]

442
00:29:37,172 --> 00:29:39,341
I can't tell you much right now.

443
00:29:41,426 --> 00:29:43,095
Why are you doing this to me again?

444
00:29:44,304 --> 00:29:45,597
You promised me.

445
00:29:45,680 --> 00:29:48,809
You said you'd explain everything
once we got out of there.

446
00:29:53,897 --> 00:29:55,190
I'm sorry.

447
00:29:55,273 --> 00:29:56,900
Is that all you can say?

448
00:29:59,277 --> 00:30:00,779
Forget it. Whatever.

449
00:30:11,164 --> 00:30:12,582
If I look in his study…

450
00:30:14,709 --> 00:30:16,628
and find whatever it is
you're looking for…

451
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:20,757
you still won't
tell me anything, will you?

452
00:30:34,146 --> 00:30:36,064
[music ends]

453
00:30:36,148 --> 00:30:37,149
[Dr. Cha] Taeju.

454
00:30:38,942 --> 00:30:39,943
[Taeju] Hi, Myeonghui.

455
00:30:41,570 --> 00:30:43,363
[Myeonghui] Good to have you back.

456
00:30:43,947 --> 00:30:45,323
I was so worried.

457
00:30:47,492 --> 00:30:49,035
Thanks for the other night.

458
00:30:50,078 --> 00:30:51,163
Don't mention it.

459
00:30:52,247 --> 00:30:53,498
I trusted you.

460
00:30:53,582 --> 00:30:56,418
I knew you'd never do anything like that.

461
00:30:59,045 --> 00:31:00,130
Are you okay?

462
00:31:00,714 --> 00:31:02,299
You don't look so great.

463
00:31:03,091 --> 00:31:04,676
Yeah, I'm good.
STYLE
::cue()

464
00:31:21,484 --> 00:31:24,446
[news anchor] The rising number of
"lonely deaths" among elderly citizens

465
00:31:24,529 --> 00:31:28,200
living alone has become
a pressing social crisis.

466
00:31:28,283 --> 00:31:29,367
Welcome.

467
00:31:29,451 --> 00:31:31,953
…build a stronger safety net

468
00:31:32,037 --> 00:31:36,583
by implementing smart care services
powered by AI and IoT.

469
00:31:36,666 --> 00:31:38,084
Reporter Kim Jisu has the story.

470
00:31:38,168 --> 00:31:41,296
[Jisu] I'm here at a smart monitoring
center operated by the local government.

471
00:31:41,379 --> 00:31:43,882
Here, you can see
real-time data tracking and status…

472
00:31:43,965 --> 00:31:45,258
Get the one next to it.

473
00:31:45,342 --> 00:31:47,010
…of elderly residents living alone.

474
00:31:47,093 --> 00:31:51,556
If the motion sensors in their homes fail
to detect movement for a set period…

475
00:31:51,640 --> 00:31:53,808
-Yeah, that one works better.
-[Manhui] This one?

476
00:31:53,892 --> 00:31:56,019
[store owner]
Yeah, the blade's way better.

477
00:31:56,102 --> 00:31:59,022
…the alarm goes off.
The government expects this initiative

478
00:31:59,105 --> 00:32:02,108
will allow local authorities
to respond to crises more rapidly

479
00:32:02,192 --> 00:32:05,278
and bridge the gaps
in our current social welfare system.

480
00:32:05,362 --> 00:32:07,572
This is Kim Jisu, reporting for NBS News.

481
00:32:07,656 --> 00:32:08,657
-Here.
-This just in.

482
00:32:08,740 --> 00:32:11,284
The criminal at the center
of national attention…

483
00:32:11,368 --> 00:32:12,786
Are you out to get somebody?

484
00:32:12,869 --> 00:32:14,746
-…of violent offenses…
-How'd you know?

485
00:32:14,829 --> 00:32:17,540
[sore owner] I've seen it all.

486
00:32:17,624 --> 00:32:19,793
It's only in their heads.

487
00:32:20,293 --> 00:32:21,878
Nobody actually has the guts for it.

488
00:32:22,629 --> 00:32:23,880
What about me?

489
00:32:24,631 --> 00:32:26,132
[store owner]
You look like a dreamer indeed.

490
00:32:28,051 --> 00:32:29,052
How much is it?

491
00:32:29,636 --> 00:32:30,929
It's 35,000 won.

492
00:32:31,012 --> 00:32:34,432
…fatally bludgeoning an acquaintance
over a financial dispute.

493
00:32:34,516 --> 00:32:37,143
Given her violent criminal history,
police are…

494
00:32:37,227 --> 00:32:39,729
She was bad news from the beginning.

495
00:32:39,813 --> 00:32:42,148
Why even bother treating trash like her?

496
00:32:42,232 --> 00:32:44,234
They should've just let her die.

497
00:32:44,859 --> 00:32:47,445
That piece of trash
doesn't deserve human rights.

498
00:32:48,905 --> 00:32:51,366
-I swear to God…
-Meanwhile, the third accomplice,

499
00:32:51,449 --> 00:32:54,452
Noh Manhui, remains at large.

500
00:32:54,536 --> 00:32:58,331
He is described as over 180 cm tall
with a heavy, muscular build.

501
00:32:58,415 --> 00:33:04,421
He was last seen wearing
a brown jacket and black pants.

502
00:33:04,504 --> 00:33:08,925
Police warn that Noh is known to be
highly impulsive and is likely armed.

503
00:33:09,009 --> 00:33:10,844
I look way better in person, don't I?

504
00:33:10,927 --> 00:33:12,345
…do not approach him

505
00:33:12,429 --> 00:33:15,432
and contact your local
law enforcement immediately.

506
00:33:16,558 --> 00:33:19,060
You think I'm just a dreamer?

507
00:33:22,731 --> 00:33:24,774
You have a terrible read on people.

508
00:33:29,779 --> 00:33:32,574
-[hammer smashing]
-[store owner screams]

509
00:33:47,964 --> 00:33:49,382
[Dr. Ko] Yeah, come in.

510
00:33:55,055 --> 00:33:56,556
Dad, I brought you some tea.

511
00:34:00,602 --> 00:34:02,937
Thank you. Leave it right there.

512
00:34:06,232 --> 00:34:08,151
How are you feeling these days?

513
00:34:09,319 --> 00:34:10,653
Yeah, I'm fine.

514
00:34:11,571 --> 00:34:13,031
Take it easy, okay?

515
00:34:16,201 --> 00:34:19,120
With everything going on at the hospital,

516
00:34:20,121 --> 00:34:21,623
you must be pretty exhausted, huh?

517
00:34:22,123 --> 00:34:23,291
I'm fine.

518
00:34:28,046 --> 00:34:30,131
-I'll leave you alone now.
-All right.

519
00:34:31,049 --> 00:34:32,300
Well,

520
00:34:32,384 --> 00:34:34,511
has Taeju been giving you a hard time?

521
00:34:35,095 --> 00:34:36,096
Sorry?

522
00:34:36,179 --> 00:34:39,599
Don't let yourself get
dragged into his business.
STYLE
::cue()

523
00:34:41,309 --> 00:34:42,519
[chuckles]

524
00:34:52,779 --> 00:34:55,615
[suspenseful music playing]

525
00:35:55,550 --> 00:35:58,011
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER
CLINICAL TRIAL APPLICATION

526
00:35:58,094 --> 00:36:01,347
[music intensifies]

527
00:36:05,310 --> 00:36:08,354
CLINICAL TRIAL APPLICATION
APPLICANT NAME: OH MINSEOK

528
00:36:11,107 --> 00:36:13,067
APPLICANT: KIM GYEONGAE
GUARDIAN: NOH MANHUI

529
00:36:16,529 --> 00:36:18,156
[Dr. Ko] So how much of a drop
are we talking?

530
00:36:19,073 --> 00:36:20,074
What?

531
00:36:20,158 --> 00:36:22,285
He was stable just this afternoon.

532
00:36:22,368 --> 00:36:24,120
Why are you telling me this now?

533
00:36:29,250 --> 00:36:31,252
Yeah, keep monitoring
Chairman Lee's vitals.

534
00:36:32,921 --> 00:36:34,798
What are you doing here?

535
00:36:35,423 --> 00:36:38,259
Oh, just picking up the tray from earlier.

536
00:36:40,512 --> 00:36:41,679
Don't stay up too late.

537
00:36:42,388 --> 00:36:43,389
Okay.

538
00:36:47,811 --> 00:36:51,231
[door opens, closes]

539
00:37:13,461 --> 00:37:15,129
[siren wailing]

540
00:37:15,213 --> 00:37:16,381
[officer] Out of the way!

541
00:37:22,929 --> 00:37:29,602
SANJEONG HARDWARE
TOOLS, BOLTS NUTS, CONSTRUCTION MATERIALS

542
00:37:30,103 --> 00:37:32,313
[camera shutter clicking]

543
00:37:36,484 --> 00:37:37,610
[Detective Oh] Hello, sir.

544
00:37:43,283 --> 00:37:44,868
Captain.

545
00:37:44,951 --> 00:37:46,911
That thing's shattered.
It's beyond recovery.

546
00:37:47,787 --> 00:37:49,038
[Dosik] Do it the old-fashioned way.

547
00:37:49,122 --> 00:37:51,082
Canvas the area.

548
00:37:51,165 --> 00:37:52,667
-Yes, sir.
-Yeah.
STYLE
::cue()

549
00:37:52,750 --> 00:37:55,336
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

550
00:37:59,215 --> 00:38:00,300
Ms. Ko.

551
00:38:01,801 --> 00:38:02,802
Dr. Cha.

552
00:38:06,764 --> 00:38:07,765
Are you okay?

553
00:38:08,766 --> 00:38:09,767
What do you mean?

554
00:38:09,851 --> 00:38:12,687
Oh, I heard about what happened.

555
00:38:13,855 --> 00:38:16,190
I can't imagine
how hard it must have been.

556
00:38:18,067 --> 00:38:19,152
I'm all right.

557
00:38:20,236 --> 00:38:23,448
It's amazing that you're already
back at work

558
00:38:24,240 --> 00:38:25,825
after such an ordeal.

559
00:38:28,745 --> 00:38:31,080
I don't think
I could've gotten through it.

560
00:38:32,957 --> 00:38:34,834
[sighs]

561
00:38:34,918 --> 00:38:36,336
Even Taeju…

562
00:38:36,920 --> 00:38:38,713
Everyone seems to be struggling.

563
00:38:40,423 --> 00:38:41,424
"Taeju"?

564
00:38:44,677 --> 00:38:46,429
Have you been talking to my husband?

565
00:38:49,682 --> 00:38:53,353
If you need someone to talk to,

566
00:38:54,062 --> 00:38:55,772
my door is always open.

567
00:38:56,898 --> 00:38:58,650
Does he stop by your office often?

568
00:38:58,733 --> 00:39:00,151
[Myeonghui] I wouldn't say often.

569
00:39:00,777 --> 00:39:06,032
But sometimes, he stops by
to talk about what's on his mind.

570
00:39:07,659 --> 00:39:08,910
About what exactly?

571
00:39:12,246 --> 00:39:16,292
Oh, I guess he doesn't tell you
about our conversations.

572
00:39:16,918 --> 00:39:19,253
Naturally, I assumed
you knew all about it.

573
00:39:20,046 --> 00:39:21,714
Is there anything I should know about?

574
00:39:23,591 --> 00:39:24,842
No, it's just…

575
00:39:26,469 --> 00:39:29,138
I think he's trying to handle
too much on his own.

576
00:39:30,139 --> 00:39:32,183
Had I known he'd never talked
to you about it,

577
00:39:32,266 --> 00:39:34,018
I wouldn't have mentioned it.

578
00:39:34,102 --> 00:39:37,939
Counseling is confidential,
so I can't really share.

579
00:39:38,564 --> 00:39:41,985
I think you guys should
sit down and talk about it.

580
00:39:43,277 --> 00:39:45,279
[elevator dings]

581
00:39:50,159 --> 00:39:51,327
I understand.

582
00:39:56,541 --> 00:39:57,959
[panel beeps]

583
00:40:03,840 --> 00:40:06,342
DIRECTOR KANG TAEJU

584
00:40:09,721 --> 00:40:12,849
NOTE: CLINICAL TRIAL APPLICANT
SCREENED OUT

585
00:40:14,600 --> 00:40:16,060
[knocks on door]

586
00:40:17,520 --> 00:40:18,730
Come in.

587
00:40:21,107 --> 00:40:22,108
Hey, Seyun.

588
00:40:24,068 --> 00:40:25,194
[door closes]

589
00:40:36,205 --> 00:40:37,498
What's this?

590
00:40:40,418 --> 00:40:41,794
It's what you were looking for.

591
00:40:42,837 --> 00:40:44,714
Documents regarding the clinical trial.

592
00:40:45,298 --> 00:40:47,300
Oh, thanks.

593
00:40:48,551 --> 00:40:52,096
And I'm sorry for getting you
involved in all this.

594
00:40:58,728 --> 00:41:00,688
I ran into somebody on my way here.

595
00:41:02,106 --> 00:41:03,274
Who?

596
00:41:08,780 --> 00:41:11,199
Someone you've been
talking to often lately.

597
00:41:13,242 --> 00:41:16,079
[melancholy music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

598
00:41:17,538 --> 00:41:18,581
It was strange.

599
00:41:20,041 --> 00:41:22,043
To find out that someone else knows things

600
00:41:23,044 --> 00:41:24,670
that you've never talked to me about.

601
00:41:26,631 --> 00:41:28,216
-That's--
-It's fine.

602
00:41:29,634 --> 00:41:31,761
I wasn't looking for an explanation.

603
00:41:31,844 --> 00:41:32,845
It's just…

604
00:41:35,431 --> 00:41:37,225
I just can't help but think

605
00:41:37,975 --> 00:41:39,894
that there's so much
I don't know about you.

606
00:41:56,536 --> 00:41:57,745
[music ends]

607
00:42:04,794 --> 00:42:07,797
[phone buzzing]

608
00:42:07,880 --> 00:42:10,091
[eerie music playing]

609
00:42:11,134 --> 00:42:12,135
What's up?

610
00:42:12,218 --> 00:42:16,013
[granddaughter] Ms. Ko just came out
of Dr. Kang's office.

611
00:42:16,597 --> 00:42:19,725
But she didn't look too happy.

612
00:42:20,810 --> 00:42:23,271
I think there's something going on
between the two.

613
00:42:24,939 --> 00:42:25,940
Really?

614
00:42:26,023 --> 00:42:28,776
Look, I can't keep this up, okay?

615
00:42:28,860 --> 00:42:32,613
I did everything that you asked. Please.

616
00:42:33,197 --> 00:42:35,408
If someone ever finds out,

617
00:42:36,200 --> 00:42:37,243
I'll be in huge trouble.

618
00:42:37,827 --> 00:42:39,078
Wouldn't you rather

619
00:42:39,996 --> 00:42:42,665
see your grandma again
while she's still alive?

620
00:42:42,748 --> 00:42:43,749
What did you say?

621
00:42:44,333 --> 00:42:47,086
You didn't do anything to her, did you?

622
00:42:48,546 --> 00:42:50,923
What are you talking about?
I didn't do anything.

623
00:42:52,425 --> 00:42:53,509
Not yet anyway.

624
00:42:54,343 --> 00:42:58,055
[breathing heavily]

625
00:42:58,139 --> 00:42:59,974
I'm not asking for much.

626
00:43:00,600 --> 00:43:03,311
I just need you to be my eyes and ears

627
00:43:03,394 --> 00:43:05,771
and tell me how those two are doing.

628
00:43:06,397 --> 00:43:07,982
But until when?

629
00:43:08,065 --> 00:43:09,525
Today.

630
00:43:09,609 --> 00:43:10,818
It'll be over today.

631
00:43:11,944 --> 00:43:13,029
You got that?

632
00:43:14,280 --> 00:43:15,448
Yeah.

633
00:43:21,662 --> 00:43:23,956
[music ends]

634
00:43:24,040 --> 00:43:26,167
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

635
00:43:38,179 --> 00:43:39,680
APPLICANT NAME: KIM GYEONGAE

636
00:43:39,764 --> 00:43:41,515
STATUS: SCREENED OUT

637
00:43:42,850 --> 00:43:45,269
[mysterious music playing]

638
00:43:47,271 --> 00:43:48,606
CLINICAL TRIAL APPLICATION

639
00:43:48,689 --> 00:43:50,524
APPLICANT NAME: LEE SEONGUK

640
00:43:50,608 --> 00:43:51,609
STATUS: ACCEPTED

641
00:43:55,363 --> 00:43:56,364
PARK DOHYEON

642
00:43:56,447 --> 00:43:57,865
ACCEPTED

643
00:43:57,949 --> 00:43:59,116
KIM HOJIN

644
00:43:59,200 --> 00:44:00,243
ACCEPTED

645
00:44:00,326 --> 00:44:02,370
OH MINSEOK
ACCEPTED

646
00:44:02,453 --> 00:44:03,663
SUNG JUIN

647
00:44:03,746 --> 00:44:05,915
ACCEPTED

648
00:44:13,923 --> 00:44:16,133
[music intensifies]

649
00:44:19,887 --> 00:44:22,640
[Gyeongae] There was
no rhyme or reason to any of it.

650
00:44:23,140 --> 00:44:27,311
-Because I'm an ex-con.
-"Ex-convict."

651
00:44:27,395 --> 00:44:29,647
It doesn't say that anywhere.

652
00:44:30,231 --> 00:44:34,819
[inhales sharply, sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

653
00:44:40,825 --> 00:44:42,326
[sighs]

654
00:44:47,540 --> 00:44:49,542
[music continues]

655
00:44:53,587 --> 00:44:56,841
CALL LOG ANALYSIS REPORT
NAME: KIM GYEONGAE

656
00:45:01,887 --> 00:45:03,014
CHA MYEONGHUI

657
00:45:09,854 --> 00:45:12,857
MAIN BUILDING ELEVATOR #3

658
00:45:22,158 --> 00:45:24,160
[no audible dialogue]

659
00:45:32,543 --> 00:45:35,546
DO NOT CROSS, UNDER INVESTIGATION
SANJEONG HARDWARE

660
00:45:36,756 --> 00:45:39,592
[car owner] I looked when you guys called,
but I wasn't so sure about it.

661
00:45:39,675 --> 00:45:41,969
Okay, give us a sec. We'll look into it.

662
00:45:44,889 --> 00:45:46,307
This freaking bastard.

663
00:45:46,390 --> 00:45:47,641
Is it him?

664
00:45:47,725 --> 00:45:48,726
Yeah, it is.

665
00:45:49,810 --> 00:45:50,811
[Hyeonsu] Wait, stop.

666
00:45:52,605 --> 00:45:53,773
What's the plate number?

667
00:46:28,516 --> 00:46:32,353
[suspenseful music playing]

668
00:46:39,443 --> 00:46:41,570
JEONGHAN GROUP
CEO LEE SEONGUK

669
00:46:42,530 --> 00:46:44,031
"Lee Seonguk."

670
00:46:44,657 --> 00:46:46,659
APPLICANT: LEE SEONGUK

671
00:46:47,868 --> 00:46:49,620
"Park Dohyeon."

672
00:46:51,122 --> 00:46:52,456
"Kim Hojin. Sung Juin."

673
00:46:52,540 --> 00:46:53,958
ILO BIO
CEO PARK DOHYEON

674
00:46:54,834 --> 00:46:56,710
CEO KIM HOJIN

675
00:46:56,794 --> 00:46:57,795
CEO SUNG JUIN

676
00:46:57,878 --> 00:46:59,588
APPLICANT: PARK DOHYEON
ACCEPTED

677
00:46:59,672 --> 00:47:01,799
APPLICANT: KIM HOJIN

678
00:47:01,882 --> 00:47:03,551
APPLICANT: SUNG JUIN

679
00:47:03,634 --> 00:47:05,386
APPLICANT: OH MINSEOK

680
00:47:06,220 --> 00:47:08,055
OH MINSEOK

681
00:47:08,139 --> 00:47:10,766
[music intensifies]

682
00:47:14,603 --> 00:47:16,647
It was all decided from the beginning.

683
00:47:17,523 --> 00:47:18,983
Those people had given up,

684
00:47:19,066 --> 00:47:22,236
but now, they're hopeful
and excited about the future.

685
00:47:23,446 --> 00:47:24,780
Couldn't you just

686
00:47:24,864 --> 00:47:28,909
let them have that hope?

687
00:47:37,960 --> 00:47:39,253
It wasn't about hope.

688
00:47:42,840 --> 00:47:44,884
It was all about money.

689
00:47:57,730 --> 00:47:58,731
[music ends]
STYLE
::cue()

690
00:48:04,278 --> 00:48:07,281
BEHAVIORAL HEALTH
CONSULTATION ROOM

691
00:48:09,074 --> 00:48:11,577
Oh, gosh.
Sorry for dropping in on you like this.

692
00:48:12,661 --> 00:48:13,662
Not at all.

693
00:48:13,746 --> 00:48:17,291
But I've told you
everything I could about Dr. Ha.

694
00:48:17,791 --> 00:48:19,251
What more would you like to know?

695
00:48:19,335 --> 00:48:24,173
Well, we took another look
at the surveillance footage.

696
00:48:25,508 --> 00:48:26,634
Okay.

697
00:48:27,635 --> 00:48:29,512
From the elevator, the day he passed.

698
00:48:31,347 --> 00:48:35,267
You were on the elevator with him.

699
00:48:36,393 --> 00:48:40,814
And I noticed he pressed
the fourth floor at first.

700
00:48:40,898 --> 00:48:42,274
[mysterious music playing]

701
00:48:42,358 --> 00:48:46,153
MAIN BUILDING E/V #3

702
00:48:46,237 --> 00:48:51,867
But then, he changed it
to the basement after you said something.

703
00:48:56,789 --> 00:48:57,790
Um…

704
00:48:58,457 --> 00:48:59,542
Did he really?

705
00:49:00,334 --> 00:49:01,502
I'm not sure.

706
00:49:01,585 --> 00:49:04,171
Yeah, that's what you said
the first time we talked.

707
00:49:04,255 --> 00:49:05,714
That you weren't sure.

708
00:49:05,798 --> 00:49:06,799
Yeah.

709
00:49:06,882 --> 00:49:11,512
And then you asked him if he was okay
because he didn't seem well, right?

710
00:49:12,721 --> 00:49:13,722
Yeah.

711
00:49:15,391 --> 00:49:17,017
But why would Mr. Ha

712
00:49:18,686 --> 00:49:20,854
switch floors after hearing that?

713
00:49:22,648 --> 00:49:23,857
Uh…

714
00:49:23,941 --> 00:49:25,317
That was before you got off.

715
00:49:27,194 --> 00:49:31,740
And after he switched floors,
you said something else to him.

716
00:49:31,824 --> 00:49:34,535
[no audible dialogue]

717
00:49:42,668 --> 00:49:43,711
[Dosik] "Well done,"

718
00:49:45,004 --> 00:49:46,005
you said.

719
00:49:46,630 --> 00:49:47,631
Tell me.

720
00:49:48,674 --> 00:49:50,217
What did you mean by that?

721
00:49:53,137 --> 00:49:55,306
[music continues]

722
00:49:57,099 --> 00:49:58,142
Ah.

723
00:49:59,184 --> 00:50:01,270
But the footage doesn't have any sound.

724
00:50:02,855 --> 00:50:06,734
How are you so sure about what I said?

725
00:50:11,071 --> 00:50:12,740
You know Kim Gyeongae, correct?

726
00:50:15,868 --> 00:50:17,786
I only talked to her during counseling.

727
00:50:19,330 --> 00:50:20,414
That's all.

728
00:50:21,165 --> 00:50:23,000
I think there's more to this story.

729
00:50:24,084 --> 00:50:28,797
You kept in touch with her
until just a month ago.

730
00:50:33,344 --> 00:50:37,264
CHA MYEONGHUI, HA JEONGSOO, NOH MANHUI,
SURVEY, CHA MYEONGHUI

731
00:50:39,391 --> 00:50:41,143
The day Mr. Ha died,

732
00:50:42,061 --> 00:50:43,395
you were in the same elevator.

733
00:50:45,064 --> 00:50:47,399
Plus, your recent contact
with Kim Gyeongae…

734
00:50:50,361 --> 00:50:51,612
Was this all a coincidence?

735
00:50:55,032 --> 00:50:56,450
[music intensifies]

736
00:50:56,533 --> 00:51:00,037
[siren wailing]

737
00:51:00,120 --> 00:51:02,122
We got the location
of Noh Manhui's vehicle.

738
00:51:02,623 --> 00:51:04,208
-He's on the move.
-Where is he?

739
00:51:04,291 --> 00:51:05,501
VEHICLE PLATE NUMBER TRACKING

740
00:51:05,584 --> 00:51:07,711
LICENSE PLATE: 61K 9024
VEHICLE DESC: SILVER SUV

741
00:51:09,505 --> 00:51:11,340
Wait, we need to notify the captain.

742
00:51:14,843 --> 00:51:17,346
61K 9024

743
00:51:32,319 --> 00:51:33,320
[music ends]

744
00:51:46,792 --> 00:51:48,043
[Gyeongae] It's you again.

745
00:51:48,961 --> 00:51:53,799
What do you have for me this time, Doctor?

746
00:51:55,968 --> 00:51:59,096
The real reason
you didn't make it onto the list.

747
00:51:59,179 --> 00:52:02,349
[laughs]
STYLE
::cue()

748
00:52:02,433 --> 00:52:05,185
Okay. So, did you find anything?

749
00:52:11,775 --> 00:52:14,862
It's a list of the top sponsors
of this hospital. Have a look.

750
00:52:20,117 --> 00:52:24,371
The other one's the list of people
who made it into the trial.

751
00:52:25,539 --> 00:52:27,416
The exact same names.

752
00:52:27,499 --> 00:52:30,252
LEE SEONGUK, PARK DOHYEON, OH MINSEOK

753
00:52:34,256 --> 00:52:36,133
It was all about money.

754
00:52:37,092 --> 00:52:39,094
Your life depended on that surgery,

755
00:52:40,637 --> 00:52:43,724
but your fate was set in stone
from the very beginning.

756
00:52:44,975 --> 00:52:48,687
You didn't lose your spot.
You just never had one to begin with.

757
00:52:49,438 --> 00:52:51,732
[somber music playing]

758
00:52:51,815 --> 00:52:52,816
But…

759
00:52:54,651 --> 00:52:58,822
Then why did they tell me
it was because I'm an ex-con?

760
00:53:08,040 --> 00:53:09,166
Who said that?

761
00:53:10,083 --> 00:53:13,962
I couldn't find any records of you
being an ex-con in the application,

762
00:53:15,339 --> 00:53:18,592
so who told you such a lie and why?

763
00:53:27,726 --> 00:53:29,978
Oh, if it wasn't Dr. Ha…

764
00:53:32,105 --> 00:53:33,273
Just my guess.

765
00:53:34,817 --> 00:53:37,861
If someone actually tried to
have you killed through Dr. Ha…

766
00:53:42,115 --> 00:53:44,910
That person is probably very happy
about this current situation.

767
00:53:48,330 --> 00:53:50,582
Do you think that person
will leave you alone now?

768
00:53:56,547 --> 00:53:58,757
[music intensifies]

769
00:54:05,597 --> 00:54:06,974
[phone buzzing]

770
00:54:08,267 --> 00:54:09,393
Yeah, Detective Jang.

771
00:54:11,895 --> 00:54:12,896
What?

772
00:54:16,108 --> 00:54:18,110
Oh, yeah, I understand. Okay.

773
00:54:28,912 --> 00:54:32,791
[phone buzzing]

774
00:54:32,875 --> 00:54:35,669
INCOMING CALL
HUSBAND

775
00:54:35,752 --> 00:54:40,924
[line ringing]

776
00:54:41,008 --> 00:54:43,927
[phone buzzing]

777
00:54:49,057 --> 00:54:51,268
[tense music playing]

778
00:55:27,554 --> 00:55:29,723
-[elevator dings]
-[automated voice] The doors are opening.

779
00:55:44,696 --> 00:55:45,822
CHAIRMAN'S OFFICE

780
00:55:46,907 --> 00:55:49,701
[music intensifies]

781
00:56:00,295 --> 00:56:02,089
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER
STYLE
::cue()

782
00:56:40,919 --> 00:56:43,422
[line ringing]

783
00:56:53,890 --> 00:56:55,892
-[elevator dings]
-[music ends]

784
00:56:59,020 --> 00:57:01,481
WING B, B3

785
00:57:09,948 --> 00:57:11,950
[sighs] Did I leave it upstairs?

786
00:57:34,639 --> 00:57:38,727
[phone buzzing]

787
00:57:41,271 --> 00:57:43,064
INCOMING CALL
HUSBAND

788
00:57:43,148 --> 00:57:44,649
[tires screech]

789
00:57:48,487 --> 00:57:52,783
[buzzing continues]

790
00:57:54,284 --> 00:57:55,494
[gasps]

791
00:58:04,252 --> 00:58:05,337
Ms. Ko.

792
00:58:07,255 --> 00:58:08,507
It's been a while.

793
00:58:13,470 --> 00:58:14,596
Where's Mr. Kang?

794
00:58:17,182 --> 00:58:18,683
MISSED CALL

795
00:58:33,406 --> 00:58:34,658
Don't move, okay?

796
00:58:36,034 --> 00:58:38,954
[gasping]

797
00:58:40,121 --> 00:58:41,373
I said don't move!

798
00:58:41,456 --> 00:58:46,294
THE HUSBAND

799
00:58:46,378 --> 00:58:49,005
[theme music playing]

800
00:59:27,502 --> 00:59:31,214
[Taeju] Who else knows about the hospital
using fetal stem cell samples?

801
00:59:32,048 --> 00:59:33,341
[Dosik] Ms. Cha Myeonghui has fled.

802
00:59:33,425 --> 00:59:35,969
-[Taeju] Myeonghui?
-[Dosik] She's a prime suspect.

803
00:59:36,553 --> 00:59:37,596
[Taeju] Was it Dr. Cha?

804
00:59:37,679 --> 00:59:40,640
The one who lied to you
that your prior got you rejected?

805
00:59:41,683 --> 00:59:43,143
Your husband should know as well.

806
00:59:43,226 --> 00:59:45,770
That you were both used and tossed aside.

807
00:59:45,854 --> 00:59:48,815
So now, you're all by yourself.

808
00:59:50,901 --> 00:59:51,902
[grunts]

809
00:59:51,985 --> 00:59:54,154
[Taeju] Who ordered you to kidnap my wife?

810
00:59:54,237 --> 00:59:55,739
[Manhui] I wasn't after your wife.

811
00:59:55,822 --> 00:59:56,948
It was you.

812
00:59:57,032 --> 00:59:58,116
On whose orders and why?

813
00:59:58,825 --> 01:00:00,827
Translated by Hyun Sik Yoon

